---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Support — Stable or Gone">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="panel hero-main">
      <div class="prompt">&gt; support registry</div>
      <h1>Support SOG</h1>
      <p>Support helps maintain a source-backed stablecoin registry: better records, more source review, clearer methodology, and more complete historical context.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel stats">
      <div class="stat"><span>Support link</span><strong>TODO</strong></div>
      <div class="stat"><span>Purpose</span><strong>registry</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel registry">
    <div class="bar">support policy</div>
    <table><tbody>
      <tr><th>Status</th><td>Support/donation link is not configured yet.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Use of support</th><td>Support is for maintaining records, reviewing sources, improving public methodology, and keeping the registry updated.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>What support is not</th><td>Support does not buy ratings, rankings, placement, recommendations, or favorable coverage.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>No investment claims</th><td>SOG does not provide investment advice, legal advice, safety scores, or buy-or-avoid conclusions.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid">
    <div class="panel mini-card"><h2>Independent registry</h2><p>SOG is designed as a public record project, not as a paid stablecoin rating service.</p></div>
    <div class="panel mini-card"><h2>Source work</h2><p>The main cost is time: finding sources, checking claims, recording uncertainty, and improving historical context.</p></div>
    <div class="panel mini-card"><h2>Secondary route</h2><p>Support is intentionally secondary. The primary product is the registry itself.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
